  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-defense art direction, disciplined red/cyan/yellow palette, and a commanding headline create a clear identity across viewports. However, desktop has a conspicuously underscaled phylogeny graphic surrounded by dead space; tablet and mobile compress dense labels, chart annotations, and explanatory copy to near-illegible sizes; mobile becomes an overly long stack of visually repetitive cards. The global header also feels clipped rather than deliberately responsive, with truncated navigation and faint labels.",
    "fix": "Enlarge or recompose the desktop phylogeny visualization, raise minimum text sizes and contrast for supporting content, simplify the mobile evidence blocks, and replace the clipped header rail with a clearer responsive navigation treatment and stronger active-state cue.",
